  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Baijnath vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 19 December, 2017 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Crr-3763-2017 sh (Baijnath Vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh) e 1 ad Jabalpur, Dated : 19-12-2017 Shri A. Singh, Government Advocate Pr Shri S.K. Mishra, counsel for the petitioner. for the a respondent/State. hy Heard on admission.",
    "facts": "h A perusal of the record reveals that the petitioner stands ig convicted under Sections 16 (1) (ka) (1) read with section 7 H (1) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and has been sentenced to undergo R.I. for a period of 6 months and fine in the sum of Rs.1,000/- with default stipulation.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the petitioner has been jail since the date of the judgment of the Appellate Court i.e. 08.12.2017; therefore, it has been prayed that the jail sentence of the petitioner be suspended. Learned Government Advocate for the respondent State has opposed the application.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the petitioner has been jail since the date of the judgment of the Appellate Court i.e. 08.12.2017; therefore, it has been prayed that the jail sentence of the petitioner be suspended. Learned Government Advocate for the respondent State has opposed the application.",
